{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 3:** Then, we rewrite all the series in the equation so that they use the same index of summation, the powers of $x$ are the same, and the indices start at the same value. In the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m = n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 4:** We consolidate all the series into a single series that is equal to $0.$ Since both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}-{a}_{n}{x}^{n}] & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[(n+1){a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n}]{x}^{n} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 5:** Setting the coefficients of the series equal to $0,$ we get the following recurrence relation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(n+1){a}_{n+1}-{a}_{n} & =0 \\\\ {a}_{n+1} & =\\frac{{a}_{n}}{n+1},\\,n=0,1,2…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the following, we'll see how to apply this recurrence relation to find the final power series solution of the differential equation." 13194139539078 17592186576411 true] [17592186362406 1064 "Let's apply the general algorithm to find the power series solution for the following equation:\n\n$$\ny' - y  =0\n$$\n\n- **Step 1:** First, we write the solution as a general power series $y =\\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a_n x^n}.$\n\n- **Step 2:** Next, we compute $y'$ so that we can substitute the general series solution into the differential equation. Computing $y',$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y