y},\\,y⟩$ does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{y}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-{e}^{y}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair $$\n\\displaystyle F(x,y)=⟨-\\frac{y}{5}+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,\\,\\frac{4x}{5}⟩\n$$ gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{5}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{4}{5},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $F(x,y)=⟨0,\\,x⟩$; $$\n\\displaystyle F(x,y)=⟨-\\frac{y}{5}+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,\\,\\frac{4x}{5}⟩\n$$ only." 13194139539078 17592186576411 true] [17592186369366 1074 "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field $F(x,y)=⟨0,\\,x⟩$ give the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Pair $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{y},\\,y⟩$ does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{y}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-{e}^{y}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair $F(x,y)=⟨-\\frac{y}{5}+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,\\,\\frac{4x}{5}⟩$ gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{5}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{4}{5},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $F(x,y)=⟨0,\\,x⟩$; $F(x,y)=⟨-\\frac{y}{5}+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,\\,\\frac{4x}{5}⟩$ only." 13194139539078 17592186576411 false] [17592186369434 1071 "![](images/39/393bed476f2e8d84fc7e5dc721d77749f7f259834e03a94a48a0853